DTSTAMP:20260610T042314Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260617T210000
SUMMARY:Give 'Em the Axe! Ladies Night at the Range in Santa Rosa
DESCRIPTION:Sonoma County Women's Wine Club (SCWWC)\nJoin us for an axe-th
 rowing session to blow off some steam. I'm super excited to be able to off
 er a ladies' Axe-throwing night in Santa Rosa. If you've ever had a curios
 ity about this fun activity\, this is your chance to find out more!\n\nWe 
 have reserved a group spot with the indoor range on a Wednesday night. It 
 will consist of an introductory lesson\, and then we all get to practice t
 aking turns. Everyone will get ample time to practice\, as they have many 
 lanes.\n\nThis event is focused on a less-competitive\, relaxed\, and ente
 rtaining atmosphere. All skill levels are encouraged. All equipment and ta
 rgets are provided by them\, and we will probably get about 1 to 2 hours t
 o enjoy ourselves.\n\nI encourage everyone to bring a bottle of wine or a 
 snack to share with the rest of the group (We usually end up with a lovely
  charcuterie and wine spread for everyone to enjoy).\n\nThere are 10 spots
  available\, guests welcome. The ladies' group lesson and event is $30 per
 son\, paid to the range. Starting March 2025\, we ask that every attending
  member pay a $1 "slush" fund fee per event so that we can build up our fu
 nds for club-related expenses\, which can be paid by Venmo or cash. There 
 may be standard liability forms to be filled out with the range. Closed-to
 ed shoes are recommended.\n\nPlease only RSVP 'Yes' if you are able to mak
 e it\, hostess Dai Phipps will be collecting a $5 fee via Venmo to hold yo
 ur spot. She will follow up with everyone who RSVP's 'Yes' via direct mess
 age or you may pay the $5 through the enclosed Venmo link. Returns cannot 
 be accommodated after the Sunday before the event. Here is the link: [www.
 venmo.com/Daima-Phipps](http://www.venmo.com/Daima-Phipps)\n\nThere is an 
 attendance policy for all our events: if you No-Show to three events\, you
  may not attend events for the next three months. Please put this event in
  your calendar so you don't miss out or get dinged. A No-Show is when you 
 are on the 'Going' list\, but do not show up.\n\nCheers\, and hope to see 
 you there!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/sonoma-county-womens-wine-club/events
 /314093470/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260402T183953Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260402T183953Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Women's Wine Club
UID:event_312553964@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260610T042314Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260625T190000
SUMMARY:THIRSTY THURSDAY New Member Social for Sonoma County Women's Wine 
 Club
DESCRIPTION:Sonoma County Women's Wine Club (SCWWC)\nThis is our regular c
 lub meeting\, held on the last Thursday of every month except for holidays
  and we are super excited! Come join us at 4th Street Cellars in downtown 
 Santa Rosa. They have generously offered to host our monthly THIRSTY THURS
 DAY social for us.\n\nIf you are new to the area\, or just looking to get 
 out of the house and make new friends\, this is the place for you. Welcomi
 ng to ALL new and (ahem\, old) members.\n\nWine is purchased by the glass 
 for a set fee of $13/$14 per glass with the variety of white\, rosé\, and
  red wines offered through 4th Street Cellars which includes tip. Fees are
  collected at the venue by Co-organizer Daima Phipps via cash\, Venmo\, or
  Paypal. You are welcome to purchase wine separately if you choose. Starti
 ng March 2025\, we ask that every attending member pay a $1 "slush" fund f
 ee per event so that we can build up our funds for club-related expenses\,
  which can be paid by Venmo or cash.\n\nThere is no food offered\, but you
  are welcome to bring an appetizer or snack to share with the group\, and 
 many ladies do. We will have time to socialize while tasting in the room u
 pstairs to the left or the outside patio if the weather is nice.\n\nThe sp
 ace has a 25 person attendee limit\, but the list is open to 40 to elimina
 te a waitlist\, and guests are welcome! Please RSVP below only if you are 
 able to make it\, we have an attendance policy: if you No-Show to three ev
 ents\, you may not attend events for the next three months. Please put thi
 s event in your calendar so you don't miss out or get dinged. A No-Show is
  when you are on the 'Going' list\, but do not show up.\n\nSee you there\,
  ready to kickoff!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/sonoma-county-womens-wine-club/events
 /312553964/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20251223T201148Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20251223T201148Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
